id=a52sxq_pure_black_theme
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: "Pure black dark mode" switch (AOSP-style black theme)
author=kusti420
description=Adds the runtime resource overlay com.k4.overlay.pureblack (product/overlay/K4PureBlack, target "android", disabled by default) and a Settings > Display switch that enables or disables it through OverlayManager. The overlay turns the dark variants of Android's surface roles (system_background_dark, system_surface*_dark) and of the dark end of the neutral palettes (system_neutral1/2_700..1000_dark), plus the legacy Material dark backgrounds, into #000000 - the same set the AOSP "black theme" implementations use. Only *_dark resources are touched, so light mode cannot change. Scope: apps and system surfaces that follow Android's dark theme colours (Google / Material You apps, AOSP-style dialogs and pages). One UI's own cards, panels and dialogs take their colours from each Samsung app and are not changed. With the Samsung "Colour palette" (wallpaper colours) switched on, SystemUI's fabricated palette overlay may take precedence over this one - not handled here.
